'''Pantorans''' were a [[Near-Human]] [[Species/Legends|species]] native to the moon [[Pantora/Legends|Pantora]], located in the [[Pantora system/Legends|Pantora system]].

==Biology and appearance==
[[File:ShenFamily-JoY.png|left|thumb|250px|Pantoran father and daughter, [[Arend Shen|Arend]] and [[Aris Shen]].]]
Pantorans were a [[Sentience/Legends|sentient]] [[Species/Legends|species]] native to [[Pantora/Legends|Pantora]],<ref name="DBPan" /> a [[Moon/Legends|moon]] orbiting the [[Planet/Legends|planet]] [[Orto Plutonia/Legends|Orto Plutonia]].<ref name="Trespass" /> They were [[Near-Human]]s, with a head, a torso and four [[Limb/Legends|limbs]]. At first glance, they only differed from the otherwise similar [[Human/Legends|Humans]] in their [[Color/Legends|blue]] skin and yellow [[Eye/Legends|eyes]].<ref name="Trespass" /> Like all [[Mammal/Legends|mammals]],<ref name="AE">''[[Alien Encounters]]''</ref> the Pantorans had [[Hair/Legends|hair]], the color of which varied between black, blue, light purple and sometimes white.<ref name="Trespass" /> The Pantorans shared many traits with other blue-skinned races, especially the [[Wroonian/Legends|Wroonian]] species, and, to a lesser extent, the [[Chiss/Legends|Chiss]],<ref name="DBPan" /> and were believed to be an offshoot of the former.<ref name="The Official Episode Guide">''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars – The Official Episode Guide: Season 1]]''</ref> The species had two [[Gender/Legends|sexes]], male and female. The Pantorans also seemed to have a greater resilience to low temperatures than Humans, since they only needed light wardrobe even under extreme cold weather conditions.<ref name="Trespass" />

==Society and culture==
Pantoran society developed on Pantora, a world located in a region flush with [[Slaver/Legends|slavers]] and [[spice merchant]]s. Constant run-ins with these types led the Pantorans to become fiercely independent and proud. While the Pantoran society was democratic, the feudal traditions of marking their foreheads, and cheeks with yellow markings to symbolize lineage persisted into the common era. These traditions spurred a cultural interest in genealogy and history, and many Pantorans cherished relics from the past such as jewelry which connected them to their noble ancestors or helmets that belonged to a great heroes of a bygone age.<ref name="EV" />

The old nation states of Pantora were unified under a democratic planetary government, the politics of which were considered an art form. Governed by the [[Pantoran Assembly/Legends|Pantoran Assembly]], the elected body was led by a [[Speaker of the Assembly/Legends|Speaker]], who balanced the power of the chief executive officer, known as the [[Chairman/Legends|Chairman]].<ref name="EV" />

Some Pantorans were known to worship an unnamed [[Moon Goddess/Legends|moon goddess]].<ref name="CW:SoI" />

==History==
===Clone Wars===
During the [[Clone Wars/Legends|Clone Wars]], the Pantorans requested, and were granted, a [[Galactic Republic/Legends|Republic]] outpost in their system as protection from the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems/Legends|Separatists]]. A Republic [[Grand Army of the Republic/Legends|military]] base was established on the frigid world of [[Orto Plutonia/Legends|Orto Plutonia]], a [[Protectorate (government system)/Legends|protectorate world]] of Pantora.

When the entire force of [[Clone cold assault trooper/Legends|clone troopers]] stationed on Orto Plutonia went missing, the Republic sent [[Jedi General/Legends|Jedi Generals]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi/Legends|Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and [[Anakin Skywalker/Legends|Anakin Skywalker]] to investigate. They were met on the planet by [[Chairman/Legends|Chairman]] [[Chi Cho/Legends|Chi Cho]] and [[Senator/Legends|Galactic Senator]] [[Riyo Chuchi/Legends|Riyo Chuchi]]. Cho immediately attempted to assert his authority, giving orders to both the Jedi and the [[Clone trooper/Legends|clone troopers]] accompanying them.

While searching the empty Republic base, Chairman Cho was convinced the Separatists were responsible; and finding a Separatist base not far away seemed to confirm his suspicions. However, after finding the Separatist base also destroyed with no evidence of contact between the Republic and CIS forces, Kenobi and Skywalker set out on [[CK-6 swoop bike/Legends|Freeco bikes]] to discover the truth. They found a tribe of [[Talz/Legends|Talz]] in the hills and discovered they were responsible for the destruction of both bases, having felt threatened by their presence. Though evidence showed the Talz had been on Orto Plutonia for some time, possibly longer than the Pantorans had claimed sovereignty over the planet, Chairman Cho insisted the Talz were trespassers and declared war with them.

[[File:POdPantorans-SoI.png|thumb|left|250px|Irate Pantorans confronting Chairman Papanoida]]
Known as the [[Battle of Orto Plutonia/Legends|One-Day War]], the battle between the Republic's soldiers and the Talz was fought in a pitched battle, instigated by Cho. The Chairman and many of his clone trooper guards were killed before Senator Chuchi, with the emergency powers granted to her by the Pantoran Assembly, was able to garner peace with the Talz chieftain, [[Thi-Sen/Legends|Thi-Sen]], assuring him that the Pantoran people would leave Orto Plutonia in peace.<ref name="EV" />

At some point around [[21 BBY/Legends|21 BBY]],<ref name="SW Annual 2011">''[[Star Wars Annual 2011]]''</ref> the [[Trade Federation/Legends|Trade Federation]] [[Blockade of Pantora/Legends|blockaded]] Pantora. Pressured by his constituents, [[Baron/Legends|Baron]] [[Notluwiski Papanoida/Legends|Notluwiski Papanoida]] listened to those who argued that the world should leave the Republic and join the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems/Legends|Confederacy of Independent Systems]] so trade could resume. However, the Baron chose to rely on Senator Riyo Chuchi, asking her to plead for assistance in the Galactic Senate. Eventually, the blockade was lifted and the Pantoran remained under the Republic's banner.<ref name="CW:SoI">{{TCW|Sphere of Influence}}</ref>

===Rise of the Empire===
[[File:Camping_Pantoran_FDSS.png|thumb|right|200px|A Pantoran Force-sensitive hiding from the Empire in the wilderness]]
When the Republic collapsed and the [[Galactic Empire/Legends|Galactic Empire]] seized control of the galaxy, Pantora was cut off from the rest of the galaxy. Struggling to come to grips with their new predicament, the Pantoran Assembly split into three factions: the Appeasers, the Republicans, and the Expansionists. The first group believed that integrating with the Empire was the only path to security and economic strength, while the traditionalist Republicans believed the Empire stood in stark opposition to the core principles and values of the Pantoran culture. The Expansionists argued that the forging of treaties with the old slaving and spice trading worlds around them would be their salvation. The Expansionists were the smallest in number, and their position was viewed as abhorrent by most Pantorans.<ref name="EV" />

Building up a small navy of volunteers, the Assembly cautiously expanded; careful to avoid drawing Imperial attention to their work. Rogue members of the Assembly began to hire [[Mercenary/Legends|mercenaries]] and make unofficial deals to free up the flow of information technologies and resources. Despite the vast resources available on Orto Plutonia, Senator Chuchi's treaty still stood, protecting the Talz from Pantoran interference. While many on the Assembly wished to respect the Treaty, others sought to educate the Talz in hopes of integrating the two societies and sharing resources.<ref name="EV" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Blue_senator_concept.png|thumb|left|150px|Iain McCaig's blue-skinned senator concept art]]
The Pantoran species was formally introduced in "[[Trespass]]," a first season episode of the animated series ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' written by [[Steven Melching]] and directed by [[Brian Kalin O'Connell]].<ref name="Trespass" /> In [[2005]], the character of [[Chi Eekway Papanoida/Legends|Chi Eekway Papanoida]] had already appeared in the novel ''[[Labyrinth of Evil]]'' and the movie [[Star Wars: Episode III Revenge of the Sith|''Star Wars'': Episode III ''Revenge of the Sith'']], but she was identified as a [[Twi'lek/Legends|Twi'lek]] at the time.<ref name="archive">{{DB|character|chieekway|Chi Eekway|oldversion=20080623065231}}</ref> Her species was later changed to Pantoran following the airing of "Trespass," which [[Retroactive continuity|retconned]] the Pantorans' first appearance to ''Labyrinth of Evil''.<ref name="dbChi">{{DB|character|chieekway|Eekway, Chi}}</ref> Similarly, the Baron N. Papanoida had first been identified as a Wroonian,<ref name="DB-Papanoida, Baron">{{DB|character|baronpapanoida|text=Baron N. Papanoida|oldversion=20051224032152}}</ref> until he was retconned as a Pantoran as well.<ref name="DBPapa">{{DB|character|baronpapanoida|Papanoida, Baron}}</ref> In [[2013]], ''Star Wars'' authors [[Abel G. Peña]] and [[Rich Handley]] identified the character of [[Kosh Kurp]] as a Pantoran, thus retconning the species' first appearance to the [[1995]] comic ''[[Jabba the Hutt: The Gaar Suppoon Hit]]''.<ref name="BRLY">{{SW|url=news/barely-tolerable-alien-henchmen-of-the-empire-part-1|series=Barely Tolerable: Alien Henchmen of the Empire|text=Part 1|nolive=1}}</ref>

The look of the Pantorans in ''The Clone Wars'' was inspired by a concept illustration of a blue-skinned Senator drawn by [[Iain McCaig]] for [[Star Wars: Episode I The Phantom Menace|''Star Wars'': Episode I ''The Phantom Menace'']].<ref name="DBPan" /> One such very early design by McCaig, dated from [[1995]], was shown in a gallery of the interactive CD-ROM ''[[Star Wars: Episode I Insider's Guide]]''. In addition to the blue skin, that drawing already featured the trademark yellow eyes and facial tattoos of the Pantorans.<ref name="E1:IG">[[Star Wars: Episode I Insider's Guide|''Star Wars'': Episode I ''Insider's Guide'']]</ref> In ''[[The Art of Star Wars Episode I: The Phantom Menace]]'', it was revealed that the blue-skinned man was based on photographer [[Greg Gawlowski]] and was meant to depict an "evil senator."<ref name="ATPM">''[[The Art of Star Wars Episode I: The Phantom Menace]]''</ref> A character of similar appearance was featured on page 172 of ''[[The Wildlife of Star Wars: A Field Guide]]'', a reference book written by [[Terryl Whitlatch]] and [[Bob Carrau]]. The individual in question has blue skin and hair, yellow eyes and facial tattoos,<ref name="WoSW">''[[The Wildlife of Star Wars: A Field Guide]]''</ref> like the Pantorans shown in ''The Clone Wars''.<ref name="Trespass" />

For "Trespass", the actors providing the voices of the Pantoran characters were requested to incorporate a [[Wikipedia:South Africa|South African]] accent for their characters.<ref name="Brian George">{{SWArchive|url=theclonewars/news/20090129.html|text=Chairman Cho: A Very Bad Man}}</ref>

Pantorans are playable characters on the massively multiplayer online [[Star Wars video games|video game]] [[Star Wars: Clone Wars Adventures (video game)|''Clone Wars Adventures'']].<ref name="SW:CWA">[[Star Wars: Clone Wars Adventures (video game)|''Star Wars: Clone Wars Adventures'']]</ref>

